    "intro_html":  "This is the pot roast every other pot roast is measured against. Chuck roast, onion, carrots, celery, potatoes, and broth, all in one vessel, cooked long enough that the meat gives up and the vegetables take on the gravy. Nothing clever, nothing trendy, just the dinner that has worked for a hundred years. Each bowl carries \u003cstrong\u003e{{protein}} grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e and {{cal}} calories for about \u003cstrong\u003e${{cost_ps}}\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost).",
